Well, shopkeepers are nothing I'd forbid my pet to kill (you can 
grab all the stuff for free, and get all the shopkeeper's 
money).  For priests, you're lucky if they're in a room with doors, 
since then you can close and lock them in.  This works in particular 
in mine-town.

Note for future reference:  A dragon is stupid enough to attack 
a blue jelly until he dies.  And he would never try his breath 
weapon for this.  *sigh*  At least it got me an amplified health 
(it's strange that one is allowed to eat pet's corpses unless 
they are cat/dog/horse ones).

> If not, is there a trick to keeping a polymorfed pet from going feral?

The trick is not to let them become feral ;-).
Usually, thery don't become feral if you're on the same level, 
so one tries to keep them at hand.  The most painful powerful 
pet I know of are liches.  First, they destroy potions with their 
attacks, second, they 'port themselves near you, even inside 
locked temples (i.e., shrines with a priest), third, you have 
to look _very_ carefully for lvl teleport traps, or else.
(It's really hard to run away from a lich, as one would do with 
other powerful pets going feral).

Lashes are important, but of course the way to go are magic 
whistles.  A non-teleporting pet can alomst always be locked 
away safely and won't mind.  One _can_ leave pets on a different 
level, if one visits this level every n turns (where n should 
be larger than 50, I guess, so visiting the lvl each 50 turns 
should be save), but one has to remember that.  It's possible 
for them to stay tame even after 500 or 1000 turns alone, but 
it's getting more unlikely very fast.

